# Important
✅ WiX Burn

Burn is a part of WiX Toolset. It’s the bootstrapper engine used to create a single .exe installer that can install multiple MSIs, EXEs, or other packages in a chain.

So:

Burn is not separate — it's built into the WiX Toolset.

You use Burn when you create a special WiX project using a <Bundle> in a .wxs file.

# The output is an .exe, not an .msi.

✔ Summary
Tool	Output	Use
WiX MSI Project	.msi	A single app installer
WiX Burn (Bundle)	.exe	A combined installer for many apps (EXE, MSI, etc.)

Got it — if your client wants a single .msi file, Burn will not work, because Burn only produces .exe bootstrapper installers, not .msi.

# which wiX Template to choose

# WIx setup Project 
A Setup Project generates a single .msi (used for installing one app).

# wiX Bootstraper project 
A Bootstrapper Project creates a .exe installer (called a bundle) that can:

Chain together one or more .msi/.exe installers

Include a custom UI, like your password prompt

Run prerequisite checks or logic before installation starts



⚠ Why This Is Important:
# WiX cannot bundle multiple .msi files into a single .msi because Windows Installer prohibits nested MSI execution (this is a Windows Installer limitation, not a WiX one).

That means:

You can’t run MSI 1, MSI 2, and install other EXEs from inside another MSI.

Only Burn (.exe) can do that chaining and sequencing.

